Fix agent toolset toggle for nested disabled_toolsets

Hermes profiles keep disabled_toolsets nested under agent: (indented), but the
reader and rewriter only matched a top-level key. As a result reading returned
an empty list and enabling/disabling a toolset was a silent no-op (it wrote the
file back unchanged).

- _disabled_toolsets: match the key at any indent and collect items indented
  deeper than the key, so the nested list is read correctly.
- _rewrite_disabled_toolsets: preserve the key's indentation and the existing
  item indentation when replacing the block, and emit "disabled_toolsets: []"
  when the list becomes empty instead of dropping the key.

Verified against pt-scanner: the Skills tab now reads the real list and the
enable/disable round-trip edits the nested block in place.

